{"user": "Is it good to get a corner early?", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T13:12:37.304590+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **a corner is almost always good**, even early, because it can **never be flipped back**.\n\nBut the key is: don\u2019t *give up* a corner by playing next to it too soon.\n\nQuick rule:\n- **Take a corner if you can.**\n- Be careful with squares next to an empty corner, especially the diagonal \u201cX-square\u201d like **b2 next to a1**.\n- A corner is strongest when it helps you build a stable edge afterward.\n\nSo: **getting a corner early is good; handing your opponent a corner early is usually bad.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T13:12:41.639237+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T13:12:43.988746+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Solution Request": 1}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Hint": 2, "Neutral Feedback": 1, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint", "Neutral Feedback"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction", "Positive Feedback"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"Gen